## SideWinder Phase 2 ##
Now that the core product (the parametric path generator) is built and works successfully, we can move to phase 2 which is expanded functionality. 
The three main issues with the tool:
- The tool has the name "Axis Spline" and not "SideWinder Paramentric Spline Tool" at the top visible to the user
- The tool cannot chain selections along otherwise valid 'discrete' paths and a sketch generated by the tool is not driven by other changes to the drawings that originally composed it. If it is possible to fully parametrically link them, do that, otherwise, just make it refresh everytime "Compute All" command is used.
- The tool is not accessible from the menus other than the utilities/add-in menu. It would be nice if it could be located on the 'create' screen in solids.
To address the first problem, we need to elimnate the mention of Axis Spline everywhere but folder names. Anything in a menu or installer that someone sees should have the branding of "SideWinder Parametric Spline Tool"
To address the second problem, we will want to simply allow chaining of selections (and perhaps even tangent selections if available) along valid paths just like is allowed in sweep operations
To address the third problem, we need to either parametrically link them, which might involve changing how the solution works entirely, but an easier way to do that altogether is to make it such that "compute all" can allow somone to refresh their parametrcially generated curve each time it is used. If none of those work, adding "SideWinder" menu to fusion and making a "Refresh Parametric Sketch" Button is a possible solution too.
